/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-sensorium/fixtures/claude-week-2026-10-07/sources/claude/7bdba225-5131-4cfb-a258-6d3e7da875f9.jsonl:2381:{"parentUuid":"a4b57376-954a-463a-8644-8ae9f1073185","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfqmATc5XSULEkd1ZWp3Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# 3.0.0 is released\n\n**https://github.com/joshuafontany/VSCode-TW5-Syntax/releases/tag/v3.0.0** — marked Latest, with `tw5-syntax-3.0.0.vsix` (124 603 bytes) attached. That file is **the artifact CI built and verified**, downloaded from the run, not a second local build.\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| `main` | `4afa852`, CI green |\n| `v3.0.0` | → `4afa852` (final seat) |\n| parent | repinned `4afa852` (`c687ab03d`) |\n| measured | 676/676 tool tests · 49/49 gates both readers · 22 files packaged, 0 strays |\n\n## The spirit's work — verified, not taken on its word\n\nIt chose **live resolution over vendoring**: `tools/gruvbox-model.js` reaches a real install the way `grammars.sh` reaches VS Code's bundled grammars, found yours at `jdinhlife.gruvbox-1.29.1` through the WSL mount, and derives the six names from whatever `.json` files sit there — never hand-listed. Absent (CI always), it SKIPs with a named reason.\n\nI checked its claims against the tree myself: base correct, no overlap with my branch, the `gate-report.js` exclusion exactly as described, and the `package-lock.json` change is a genuine correction — the lockfile still said `2.3.0`.\n\nWhat it measured: `a CamelCase link` vs prose reads **4/65** bundled, **0/6** gruvbox. The `variable` family reads **59/65** (20 quiet) bundled, **6/6** (0 quiet) gruvbox — gruvbox always actively paints `variable`. **No floor moved**, because `gruvbox-report` is ruled a non-gate; the 49-gate roster didn't change at all.\n\nIt also handed back a finding worth keeping: **`resolveSeed()` breaks from a worktree** (it walks `__dirname/../../bags/`), so a worktree-isolated sweep reads `sigil-shape`/`sigil-vocabulary` as drifted for that reason alone. Pass `LARES_SEED` explicitly, as `TW5_PATH` must be. Recorded.\n\n## The package audit found worse than you asked about\n\n`tests/`, `corpus/`, `editions/` were already excluded — never leaking. What was: **`.claude/worktrees/` — 128 MB, 10 760 files, 1 507 executable**, and it had already disabled the guard that would have caught it by overflowing `execFileSync`'s 1 MB buffer into a false \"vsce unavailable\" skip. The package is now 22 files with a gate refusing the twenty-third. Two more faults fell out: walkers pruning `.worktrees` but not `.claude`, and `ThirdPartyNotices.txt` minting a phantom ledger `otices.txt`.\n\nMy first cure for the skip was also wrong and CI said so — I inferred absence from a failure's message, which redded every leg that has no `vsce` (all of them; only the `package` job fetches one). Now it asks `vsce --version` directly. The CI-side bound lives in `package-contents` in the `package` job, over a real .vsix.\n\n## Three things left for you\n\n1. **Marketplace publish** — needs your PAT, so it's yours:\n   `! cd VSCode-TW5-Syntax && npx --yes @vscode/vsce publish --packagePath /home/joshu/.claude/jobs/86a17260/tmp/release/tw5-syntax-3.0.0.vsix`\n2. **The submodule is now on `main`** — I switched it off `release/3.0.0` to verify the merged tree. Say the word if you want it back.\n3. **The release workflow** you asked about — I'll write it as its own PR whenever you like; the design stands as described, keyed on the tag, reusing `package`'s artifact, with the Marketplace step behind an Environment gate.\n\nStill owed and unchanged: the unterminated-italic finding donated upstream, 3.0.1 phases 3–6, and your ruling on which `lar:` querystring form the corpus adopts."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5655,"cache_read_input_tokens":373921,"output_toke