cific recommendation per branch**: land it (and onto what), salvage one named piece from it, or drop it — with the measurement or the citation behind your call.\n\n# CONTEXT THAT WILL SAVE YOU TIME\n\n- **`feature/base-scheme-punctuation` almost certainly touches a REFUTED area.** The operator ruled during 3.0.0 that the base grammar's scheme runs stay FUSED: splitting `://` and path separators into `punctuation.*` in the BASE grammar was measured and refused, because any `punctuation.*` leaf lets a theme's blanket rule recolour the span, and the legibility floors forbade the drop. Verify that against the real commits and the record rather than taking my word for it — if the branch does something else, say so.\n- **`scout/uri-measure` sounds like a measurement scout**, and its findings may already be recorded in `corpus/`, in `LEDGER-3.0.0.md`, or in the grammar's own dated comments. A scout branch whose *findings* already landed as rulings carries nothing even if its code never merged.\n- The two readers: the fork at `TW5_PATH=/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/TiddlyWiki5` (canonical) and the pinned `TW5_PATH=$PWD/node_modules/tiddlywiki`. **Pass `TW5_PATH` explicitly** — from a worktree the resolver silently falls back to the pinned package. Pass **`LARES_SEED=/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot.mem`** too if you run any seed-reading gate, or you will read a false drift.\n- Gate sweeps are heavy. Run at most ONE at a time; concurrent sweeps once drove this machine's load to 9 and got a spirit killed.\n- Do not spawn helper agents. Do all of it yourself. Leave nothing running at handback.\n- **Change no tracked file, make no commit, push nothing, delete no branch.** If you want scratch space, use your own worktree.\n\n# WHAT TO HAND BACK\n\nPer branch: what it changed (with the diff's substance), whether it is superseded, whether it still applies cleanly, and **land / salvage / drop with your reason**. Then one short c