bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/i1-intent-lane.mem:36:* ''The operator's word.'' A `release`, `cancel` or operator `supersede` that outranks claims signs under the persona root (the op-key under the face's KEL, verified at the entry's `epoch`). An issuer's own atom may supersede or cancel its own intent, a claimant releases its own claim, and any other atom's release refuses by name. A device that holds no root asks the root's hearth through an `asks` entry.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/i1-intent-lane.mem:47:# ''Claims, release, causal voids ~ BUILT.'' A takeover fences a zombie claimant's act on a fenced effect and an idempotent effect converges; the read never touches a clock (the tests install throwing spies); a root-signed release steers the read and an atom that is neither issuer nor root releases nothing; a device that merges a void declines and an unbounded intent is honored (`intent-read.test.ts`, `intent-issue.test.ts`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:49:* ''Entries append, never edit'', each signed by the atom of the device that writes it (a far agent's by its own key, #/the-far-agent). Kinds:
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:68:# ''A claim steers effort'' on a long act: a claimant appends `claim`, then its outcome or `release`. Another device may append `takeover` naming the claim; a fenced effect accepts an act only from the current claim, and an idempotent one converges either way.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:76:* ''A claim never expires.'' It ends by its own outcome, by `release`, or by `takeover`. A device MAY suspect a claim stale by its own local elapsed time and decide to try a takeover; no clock value enters the log or settles anything.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:78:* ''The operator's release always wins'': a `release` or `cancel` signed for the face outranks any claim, by authority, never by order.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:91:* It signs an `intent` and hands it to a ''relay seat'': a vessel of the face with a door off the local socket, opened per face, ring-gated and off by default. The relay verifies the chain and appends the entry carrying the AGENT's signature; it countersigns only its admission.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:28:(#/cold-start), the rulings (#/rulings), the design decisions that shape unbuilt work (#/decisions),
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:80:* ''No global now'' and ''the fence'': #/rulings.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:85:* ''Early alpha'': no back-compat, no shims, no legacy recovery; a stale thing aligns to the current frame and grammar, and a third human's arrival ends that line (#/rulings, the fence) (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/wild-bytes">>). Derive, never enumerate. One function, one relation.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:93:<<~ ahu #/rulings>>
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:146:* ''Locality law'': an unattended ember answers on the local link only, and only where the hearth holds a hardware freshness anchor the ember checks on each ask (#/rulings, the ember's key at rest); a relay pin wants an attending hand. The vessel rests at the floor and raises when t embers answer; the raise lapses by non-renewal, which reads as the raise's next causal boundary (#/rulings, how a raise lapses).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:188:* ''Gate keys come in three tiers'': a floor route's keys derive from the floor key, and a sovereign route's from the sealed custody root (operator ruling); the serving route's bundle derives from SK, a third tier that leaves those two untouched (#/rulings, the ember's serving gate). A faceless place takes a fourth arm at the gate, the place arm, and a session opens before its certificate. The floor key rests outside the vessel key, and the face proof names what a holder of the disk without the passphrase reaches and never reaches (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:199:* ''Each browser tab asks for its own unlock.'' A tab that attaches to the shared holder opens the keystore by its own ask of the person; the holder carries no unlock between tabs. The reason reads off the session law: a session wears its own face, so each tab answers for its own opening (#/rulings, a session wears the face). The ask admits a tab to its face's open hive and derives no key: the holder keeps a face's keys while some session of that face stands unlocked, and the last to close locks it (operator, 2026-10-18; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/session-unlock-2026">> #/what-both-faces-hold). Row `B1` carries the build.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:218:* ''The ember's key at rest'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). A separate serving key (SK), the fifth custody class `serving`, wrapped by the vessel key and by ember slots, seals the serving rows alone, and the serving tier holds no minting secret: a walker's grant checks under a public half, a shape the hosted road's re-cut lands before the ember's walker arm. An unattended answer (any slot that answers without a person's confirm on the ember) needs a freshness anchor a disk copy cannot carry, a hardware-sealed hearth key whose attestation the ember checks on each ask; without one every ember slot answers only on a person's confirm, threshold two buys a second confirm and never an unattended raise, and after any counted removal a bare deny-only `sk-rotation-owed` mark refuses every ask until SK rolls, a mark a rolled-back disk copy can omit. ''For the operator'': a hearth that holds no hardware anchor raises only on a person's confirm. The reason: a key that opens serving state opens nothing beside it, and a copied disk replays any freshness it carries; the ruling flips on a threat review showing the serving rows hold nothing a thief can use even before the grant re-cut (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-table">>; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ember">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:230:* ''Engine cadence'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). Cadence keeps its own lineage and threshold, apart from every seat key. A Nexus's joint founding cites one cadence inception that names each founder's hearth, the device that bears the reboot, as a holder; a household seed carries none, since its one holder bears its reboots. Each hearth mints its cadence key at random on the device, never derived from serving or floor material, and keeps it, with its next-key commitment, as a `cold` row under the vessel key that unwraps per act; no sixth custody class and no extra card at the founding. A holder may later rotate onto a cold card by its own choice. Each island pins one engine epoch, and one daemon hosts two epochs only as two separately pinned islands. The reason: the people who bear a reboot decide it, and a seat-holder who runs no hardware forces no one's restart. The ruling flips on a cadence act that must run unattended where a per-act unwrap cannot (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/contract">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:248:* ''The channel of intent'' (operator, 2026-10-20: //"Approve your leans, land the full models into the architecture now"//). The daemon wiki keeps working memory; a face's intents travel on that face's own intent plane, `@intents-<tag>`, a fifth face plane beside the four; a vessel's own records rest in its daemon bag, unmirrored; the face's pins rest in the face's custody and `@persona`. The approved leans: the plane stands from the first landing, never staged in the daemon bag; the winner reads by the intent's own preference list, else the lowest `H(atom ‖ intent id)`, and never elects; a single-effect fleet-wide verb never addresses "any device", and a human answer may name its executor; a claim never expires, a device's staleness stays a local suspicion, and the operator's release always wins; an `every` intent reaches a later-joined device unless its bound names a roster edge; a far agent reaches the plane through a relay seat, opt-in per face and ring-gated, its research before its build; an intent voids by supersession, a revoked delegation, a passed roster edge or the operator's cancel; compaction folds by the operator's act, never a timer; a local verb that touches its own vessel alone bypasses the plane and leaves its receipt in that vessel's bag. The plane carries a hand's decisions that cross devices, never its motion (the rubric, <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane">> #/the-rubric). Row `I1`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:281:* ''The socket's handshake changes once.'' R-WIRE and the face proof build as ONE wire train: the signed admit, then the fleet-join door, then one socket cutover (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof">>). The tree between those steps reads no earlier shape; it stands as a build order, never a compatibility mode.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:305:(#/rulings) bounds the whole road: every slice that changes a shape lands before the second operator seats a key in the first Nexus.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:314:* ''The receipt ledger's direct leg'': the three receipts of #/rulings stand where a CLI meets its vessel (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/receipt-ledger">>). The leg across a herm rides THE WIRE (`W12` of #/the-loops).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:332:* ''No keyring stands'' (operator ruling, #/rulings): the code holds no per-Nexus convergence secret. No custody row, seat mint, admission delivery or charter commitment carries one, and a persona admission's signed transcript names no keyring digest. A private body seals under its bag's content key, which reaches its readers through a lockbox (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/sealed-store#/keys">>). A seat's act and a roll mint nothing beside the charter epoch. The same ruling's standing law binds every later slice: let a counter, wherever one appears, order one writer's own emissions only; keep the face at the session capability; keep every verified fork head visible; retain by causal evidence.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:365:* ''The cadence inception'' cited once by a joint Nexus founding, never by a household seed: its shape stands in <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/contract">>, and its holders stand ruled (#/rulings; `K9`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:379:* ''R-KAHU'' stands witnessed: a two-of-two charter whose seats live on two vessels opens, cosigns and lands a cabal admission and a promotion, each vessel under its own scratch root (`nexus-cabal.test.ts`, `nexus-promote.test.ts`). The co-signed `keptBy` fills the realm's steward map (#/rulings).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:412:* ''What blocks rung 3 onward'': rung 3 waits on ONE FACE. Rung 4 waits on HARBOR's household HTTPS, on the KAHU PLANE's grant for a foreign leaf, and on browser custody: a browser leaf holds a passphrase or paper slot before it holds a persona root (#/rulings).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:459:* `K15` One hive per face (#/rulings, 2026-10-18): each PersonaGroup owns its Keyhive identity, event store, registry, archive and content-key seat, and no identity stands above them. Build order, each step red-first: (0) before bytes move, the custody contract of <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero">>: the node and browser row census sorted D, F or S, the FCK key class, each face's own slot tree and recovery route, the carrier binding of face, row name and kind, and the overwrite contract generalized to a row-class key (#/rulings, a face's custody rows seal under its own key; a shared act never makes a shared secret) (the node census built, PR #70: each carrier row names its target classes, a LEAD mark and its open joint, and `encodeCarrierContext` spells the D and S seal context; the archive-row-selector joint traced and held open, PR #71: no archive site hands its row an authenticated PersonaGroup); (1) a substrate probe that two Keyhive instances in one process hold apart under interleaved acts, a reboot and a cross-read (measured: isolation holds, `packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/two-hives-one-process.probe.test.ts`), then a face context with its own store, registry, archive and key seat; (2) the face as the sole owner of its identity and group, the vessel's delegation gone from every face-bearing event (built, PR #68: `makeFaceBagDoor`, `faceOwnerVerifier`, a two-face event-byte capture its red, `W25`'s probe its regression), and 2b, a bag keeping one Document across boots (built, PR #68: `registerBagsDurably`, its record on the daemon doc for the vessel's ground and on each face's plane for that face's bags); the door grants the face's group before it records a Document (PR #69), so a crash between them re-enters to the same end; (2c, operator ruling 2026-10-19; built, PR #79) the atom cut: a random atom per (vessel, PersonaGroup) under that face's FCK signs every act on the face's behalf on node and browser, the place signer keeps the floor's duties alone, the wire subjects and verifiers move together, and its genesis, admit and founding-bootstrap deltas ride `X0` by `genesis/unbaked.json`, red-first on a thief holding the place seed deriving no veil and opening no group secret; on the local presence channel the session wears the mounted face, so a verb's presenter derives from the island's own atom and never from the CLI's unsigned `requestedBy`, the floor presents the place for floor acts alone, and a verb that names another face refuses by name (#/rulings, a session wears the face, 2026-10-11; a published atom key would link face and vessel on a wire); (3) sessions and registries routed by one face, no union, with `F6` slice three's asker-seals beside it, each sealer holding its row class's key (built, PR #81: the browser house keys by (PersonaGroup, persona root), the island proves each face through `gate:clear` while the holder holds no key, the island reads the fleet board's dyad itself, a fresh group mints a fresh atom, founding seeds key by their ask digest, and the node keys its atom and veil-archive rows by PersonaGroup digest; the daemon's last unions ride step 6); (4) content keys and removal per face, `K12`'s fresh group inside it; (5) a one-face restore and a herm that carries yet authors nothing; (6) the fence migration, identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, and archive and custody formats together, under one identity model (#/rulings, sync carries, verification decides: the sealed anchor, the signed `@persona` log, verified projections): each D row (the atom's seed, its archive) seals under its face's FCK, where the node now seals them under the seated vessel key, and keys by its PersonaGroup, as the node's atom and veil-archive rows and the browser's atom row already do, where the browser's veil archive still keys by handle index. The isolation red: unlock face A alone, bypass every route, and try to open and replace B's occupied carriers with every key A holds, the S key included; each open fails, B's bytes stand unchanged, and A's bundle restored on a fresh vessel holds nothing of B. Lead: DreamNet-Wright after `W26`'s floor slice lands. K, W. Wave C (step 6 under the identity anchor, `readFace` as the one door with its census) landed in PR #86 on 2026-10-23. `K15-H` (the Handle owner rides the anchor, the row in `docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane`) landed in PR #88. Wave D (the FCK fence, its eight slices whole, kit `docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane`) landed in PR #95 on 2026-10-26: each face seals its D rows under its own FCK, unlocks apart, bundles and restores alone, lifts its anon veil on join, and seats when its grant arrives. `K17`'s realm leg (`docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane`) landed in PR #97 on 2026-10-26.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:460:* `B1` Browser custody. The custody API stands specified in `browser-custody.ts`: a passphrase or paper (2-of-3) slot binds the slot tree, the device seed and every Keyhive Archive move into sealed carriers through the mesh's one sealed writer, a wrong route refuses and changes no byte, a locked keystore refuses `sealed-locked` before any mint, and the clear-password act asks through the confirm door and answers only to a literal yes. The boot stands (PRs #48 and #61): the vessel lock gives back on a throw and a `sealed-locked` boot retries in the same page, the web boot asks the unlock through its own form, the clear verb answers `asks` and calls no door before a literal yes, the wiki's `tm-clear-password` road asks through TW5's confirm road and writes no synced tiddler, the question names what it clears, and a declined unlock retries in the page. Under #/rulings (a shared act never makes a shared secret) the browser holds no vessel key, so the clear names one face and clears that face's rows, built inside `K15` steps 0 through 3. Owed: the persona roots, which still rest in the clear outside the tree, sealed under it, with the mint refusing until a slot binds (#/rulings); the browser's vessel-key rotation; and the passkey slot, after its derivation gets measured (`B3`) and never alone. Each tab asks for its own unlock, and the ask admits that tab to its face's open hive while the holder keeps a face's keys only while some session of that face stands unlocked (#/rulings, 2026-10-18; the research and its leads at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/session-unlock-2026">>). Built with `K15` step 3 (PR #81): the holder answers a port only for a session it admitted, an unadmitted port asking for a sealed body refusing by name, and the last session of a face to close locks that face's hive; the production holder lifecycle stays a named skip on every engine until Wave C's one SharedWorker per house. B.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:467:* `F11` The hands: the watcher as a leasing session, the seat under a standing grant, the Mask as a record field, door parity at the session (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/the-hands">>). An agent's dissent drafts and a person's direct ask edits (#/rulings, 2026-10-16). O1.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:472:* `G34` A removal no reader can keep refuses by name (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/automerge-doc-store">>). The store lands a based removal a concurrent writer overrode, then surfaces it to a listening reader alone: with no parallel-drafts reader it drops the surfacing with no word, and a reader that throws earns one console line while the write stands (`automerge-doc-store.ts`, `parallel-drafts.ts`). Owed: the refusal by name before any change lands, wherever no reader stands or every reader failed, with the store authoring no draft of its own; and the durable conflict handle the refusal carries (the document, the removal's request id, the conflicting change and head identities, never the hand's text), at a home where a hand whose editor went offline finds it again. G.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:473:* `G35` The disk watcher's standing instruction (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/disk-projection#/projection-law">>). Owed: the instruction as a record the operator signs by a human route, naming one bag, a path pattern and a per-wave count ceiling, which no automated seat signs; the watcher's settle of each pending removal it covers through the shore's removal door; the audit row that names the instruction a removal rode; `lares shore restore` over a settled removal; and a mass vanish past the ceiling, a standoff, or a removal outside the pattern left pending for a person (`packages/lares-cli/src/commands/watch.ts`, `shore-verb.ts`, `disk-projector.ts`). G.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:482:* `K16` The Teshima Family Council (#/rulings, 2026-10-18; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm">>), `K15`'s acceptance story. Kalani founds a private council; Leilani joins it with two of her three faces. Red-first, after `K15`'s face context: (1) the council's hive as a Keyhive group holding no key of its own, its members the chosen faces' own identities; (2) an invite walks Leilani to the door, the threshold grafts each chosen face, a face leaves by its own act, and another's removal rides `kapae` or a fork by omission; (3) a member face's photo lands in its working layer of the council wiki and reaches the council's canon by `MOVE` (`W27`); (4) both chosen faces read it, the face kept back reads nothing and learns nothing, and no event in the council's history names a creator or issuer that ties two of Leilani's faces together; (5) a herm carries the sealed book and authors nothing (`K15` step 5). The e2e set stands four vessels: Kalani's, one per chosen face of Leilani's, and a herm. The e2e set walks the council at one hearth first: Kalani's seed charter holds the realm and Leilani's chosen faces walk there as guests, no Nexus founded (#/rulings, one charter). The two-hearth council follows, under the Nexus the two found, and there the member consult that lets a realm's documents cross between two operators reads a root map nothing fills (cabal-realm #/many-realms, owed), and the climb from seed charter to Nexus re-pins the realm by a named act (owed). Open joints: a quorum Handle with a seated key stands only where the council signs as one name, and that key signs collective acts alone, reaching no member's hive (#/the-steward-signer, owed). K, W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:484:* `P9` The re-seal proof and the fork-resolve act stand ruled (#/rulings): the re-seal record builds with sealed-store step three, the fork-resolve act in train N.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:488:* `W12` The herm route for cancel and the three receipts, as ruled (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/receipt-ledger#/the-relay-leg">>); no code asks, cancels or answers across a herm. Owed, with `W9`: the ask, the cancel and the vessel's answer as a tagged inner frame under the sealed sibling session's own seal, the vessel reading that session's proof as the asker's; the herm's bare delivery note inside the session, bound to the ask's unique request id and the session's causal position, attesting transit and never execution; and the rule for which verbs a sibling's standing reaches across the session (`sibling-channel.ts`, `uds-channel.ts`). W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:489:* `E2` The serving key's custody and its unattended road (#/rulings, the ember's key at rest; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-table">>). Built: the fifth class `serving` in the carrier table, read by the census and `vault status`; SK minted at the founding; `sk-slots` with the vessel key's entry, opened at every human unlock and re-wrapped by a vessel-key rotation. Owed: the serving rows under SK and SK's own rotation; no minting secret in any serving row; the anchor path, where an ember slot answers unattended only against a hardware-sealed hearth key whose attestation the ember checks on each ask; the confirm path, where every slot of a hearth with no such anchor answers only on a person's confirm and threshold two asks a second confirm, never an unattended raise; and the bare deny-only `sk-rotation-owed` mark that any counted removal sets and that refuses every ask until SK rolls (`vault-carriers.ts`, `keyslot.ts`, `custody-seat.ts`). E.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:490:* `E3` The serving gate's tier (#/rulings, the ember's serving gate; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>). Owed: a third tier name in the route type, its bundle derived from SK under its own registered domain, its pin, and a pin's move by a signed causal event or a verified key-history step alone, with no quiet period that ages a pin out (`gate-bundle.ts`). E.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:491:* `E4` The raise's commit point and its lapse (#/rulings, how a raise lapses; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor#/the-shape">>). Owed: the count spent at the raise ledger's durable commit, before SERVING composes, so a crash before the commit spends nothing and serves nothing and a crash after it burns the raise; and the raise's lapse at a lock, a restart, a human unlock or a counted removal, with no timer and no heartbeat that ends it (`custody-seat.ts`, the raise ledger's writer). E.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:493:* `H8` The grant's signed shape and public-half verifier stand specified in `walker-grant.ts` (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ember#/the-tiers">>). Owed: the live roll that derives grant public halves for serving rows inside H's one act cut, before E's walker arm. H.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:511:* `W26` The system wikis release and every other wiki reads the floor (#/rulings, 2026-10-16). Slice 1 stands (PR #49): genesis carries the first floor, its manifest and the `lares` and `lararium` snapshots by CID, and `@oracle` reads that floor by CID. Slice 2 stands (PR #52): each vessel's system, crossroads and realm pointers rest in its own `@catalog`, and nothing writes the shared `@oracle` after genesis (`oracle-doc-no-writer.test.ts`). Slice 3 stands (lane `--w26-floor-3`): the founding lands the counted 1-of-1 Kahu admission for persona zero's group (`landFoundingAdmission`) and registers `lares` and `lararium` as realm bags of the hearth's realm under persona zero's per-Nexus key (`landKahuRealm`); `kahuCabalCanonAccess` has its production caller (`kahuReachSourceOf`); the keel mounts only what the realm names, the registered bag set and the `bags/` mirrors follow, and no catalog row names a system bag. Slice 6 stands: one predicate (`requireKahuReach`) guards the residency reactor, meme put and delete, draft placement and a realm steward's write, and the keyholder island's verifier carries it for `--in-wiki` verbs. Slice 4 stands: the release (`floor-release`: body, CID, steward seal by a seated Kahu key, the cabal's high-impact approval of the manifest's exact bytes, the charter's epoch lineage), the chain fold, `lares nexus release`, the porch (`GET /floor/<Nexus AID>`, `/cas/<cid>` for the head's blobs), the browser's verified read, and the flow map's own `flow-pointer` domain in place of the retired `oracle-pointer`. The build runs six slices in order, under the architecture of #/rulings (2026-10-18), its shape and evidence at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane">>: (1) the floor manifest and its read-face, genesis baking the first floor; (2) each vessel's pointers leave the shared document for its bootstrap, re-cutting `W21`; (3) the Kahu realm holds the live system documents, and a one-seat founding lands its 1-of-1 Kahu admission; (4) the release answer on the crossroads, folding `P8`; (5) the accept act per (face, Nexus), which follows Wave C's face context since its accepted floor rests as a face's D row; (6) reach into system canon refuses every hand outside the cabal. OWED: a browser Kahu hand rides Wave C's face context (the browser composes no board reader and reads as a stranger, fail closed); a sibling device of a seat-holding face reads the floor until that context carries the charter and the board to it; the carriage `canon` names (`device-admit.ts` `admitCanonDocs`, the browser's `hearth-canon`) read rows nothing writes now, and retire with `W21`'s rest. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:520:* `W29` The place signs by a scoped signer under a pre-rotated KEL (#/rulings, the place signs by a scoped signer, 2026-10-19; kit <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane">>): built, PR #98, 2026-10-26. One KEL grammar (`vessel-kel.ts`, beside `persona-kel` and `handle-kel`): the inception seats the online signer and commits a cold next-key digest; a rotation reveals that key, which signs it, seats a replacement signer and commits a fresh next key; no interaction events. Every founding door, node, hearth, herm kindle and browser alike, mints the armed inception and lands no byte before the founding card reads back through the `PlaceFoundingCard` port, and the cold seed rests on no file. `lares vessel rotate` runs the card ceremony: it verifies the old card against the head, reads the replacement card back, then stages, publishes and reconciles under one custody claim, and a restart never invents a successor. Peers learn the head from the Nexus carriage board and an offline herm from the carry bundle; one fold, bounded at 64 rows and 8 pieces of fork evidence per AID, refuses a gap, a rollback and a fork. The five floor duties sign and verify `len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage`. A seed census names every raw-seed consumer and fails on a new one. Owed: a browser ceremony UI that seats a card (until it lands, the browser's KEL door refuses by name and a browser leaf holds no place KEL); the seed's other reach, K15's bonds, named in the census. Since `W14`–`W16` (PR #100), the floor pin duty and the carrier seal resolve their signer at the head (`verifyPlaceDutyAtHead`, `verifyCarrierContractAtHead`), and a flow pointer reads its publisher off the verified head. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:570:* `K13` The sealed outbox (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-table">>). Parcels rest sealed under random names in the `outbox` class. Owed: carriage shipping, idempotent receipt and local delete after ship. K.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:571:* `K14` The restored face's provisional standing (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-restore">>). The mark, guardian or chair view, confirm verbs and three authority-changing refusals stand. Owed: provisional guards at the root-signed crossing, edge kapae, device admit, two-founder act and session signer's authority purpose; a sibling view needs independent proof; the guardians' recovery path where every party stays unreachable. K, W, N.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:574:* `P8` One public answer per Nexus, signed by the steward: the floor release answer, built as `W26`'s release slice (#/rulings, 2026-10-18): the body, the steward's seal, the approval and the porch stand (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu">> #/floor-release). The domain's Handle table stays here, off the ceremony's chain by ruling. P, W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:588:* `F6` The browser holder as owner, with unicast replies. Slice one stands (PR #56): a closed routing table (`holder-routes.ts`) sends each island message to exactly one port, a reply by its request id, camera traffic by its lease, the island's own asks to its owner port, and drops a kind with no route by name. Slice two stands (PR #58): every tab-to-holder message rides a random owner epoch, a session and a generation, and the holder refuses a stale or unknown one by name to that port alone; `session:open` with its face waits on `W4`'s face supplier. Slices three and four move the Repo and the daemon kernel into the holder; their sealed writes go to the asker (#/rulings, the asker seals). Slice three stands with `K15` step 3 (PR #81): the holder routes each sealed write to the session that caused it, and Chromium, which exposes no nested Worker inside a SharedWorker, takes the dedicated-worker floor, its swap waiting for the worker's `ready` before it replays the manifest and retiring the crossing it replaces. Slice four stays owed. O1.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:634:* Guardian count and threshold remain with the operator (#/open); bundles carry enrolled guardian sets and the restore checks them (#/rulings).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:655:* `E1` The ember: the serving tier under its own key, the ember pin, the raise with its count and record, four roads of removal (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/ember">>). Its three questions stand ruled (#/rulings), and `E2` to `E4` carry what each ruling owes. E.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:658:* `W21` A joinee mounts the hearth's `@lararium` corpus read-only beside its own, while the oracle plane never crosses (#/rulings, 2026-10-16). Each vessel's pointers rest in its own `@catalog` (PR #52), so a joined vessel's pointer no longer replaces its hearth's, and `shared-oracle-doc.probe` holds that two synced vessels each keep their own. The rest rides `W26`'s floor slices: a joinee reads its hearth's floor by the release and its CIDs (slice 4), where slice 5's accept act moves its pin; a sibling device of a seat-holding face reads the floor until Wave C's face context carries the charter and the board to it, and `device-admit.ts` states the law. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:659:* `W25` The carried bag event names its creator in the clear, where the WHO plane's veil-born group hides it: measured red (`packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/bag-event-creator.probe.test.ts`, lane `--w26-own-canon`); `K15`'s step 2 hides it, since no vessel-wide identity then creates a face's bag (#/rulings, 2026-10-16 and 2026-10-18). W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:660:* `W27` A write reaches its wiki's working layer (#/rulings, 2026-10-18). Built (PR #55): `LOAD` into a canon bag refuses, naming the promotion it owes, while genesis and founding seed through their own named door; an act aimed at a bag opens the bag's own wiki, its recipe record or the floor, through one mesh record-or-floor export the surface recipe and the node's open and act paths share, and lands in its working slot; a mount that cannot stand refuses by its cause; the daemon wiki keeps the daemon's own reach. `W24` walks it. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:662:* `K17` The edge frontier (#/rulings, the edge frontier, 2026-10-20). Red-first: the frontier certificate and its verifier on node and browser alike; the signed empty genesis at every founding; registration of a raise into its signer's next frontier; the widening reader (admit, grant, a content-key seal) acting as of a qualifying frontier and waiting as unknown otherwise; the admit bundle carrying the frontier and its snapshot; the reader persisting its highest accepted head. Reds: a withheld first raise, a deleted local raise, a stale clean frontier, two conflicting frontiers, a missing snapshot, a concurrent raise and lower, an epoch rollover. Beside Wave C, on the spine. K. The fleet board's frontier stands built with Wave C. The realm leg, K17-R (kit `docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane`, the operator's rulings on forks 3 and 4, 2026-10-22), landed in PR #97 on 2026-10-26: one lease law, so a Nexus or realm lease rises only on a charter quorum's signed advance read under its seal-epoch lineage and the unsigned max-register retires with no reader left; each voucher signs its own hand's frontier; a seal roll signs every anchored realm's head under the new epoch; a split-seat cosign carries its head; and the realm admit bundle carries the board's acts, frontiers and snapshots, so a joiner holding no board acts as of them. The closed roster's window passes to `K18`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:663:* `I1` The face intent plane (#/rulings, the channel of intent, 2026-10-20; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane">>). Build order, each step red-first: `@intents-<tag>` minted by the PersonaGroup with its entry kinds (intent, outcome, asks and answer, claim, release and takeover, supersede and cancel), each signed by its device's atom and its id a content hash; stand-down and the three verb classes, with a single-effect verb addressed to "any device" refused at issue; the read-side winner; causal voids and the operator's release; the face-join summons moving off the daemon doc onto the plane, which closes two hearths of one face, beside the CLI naming its face per invocation; the daemon wiki's view pane; the rubric's witness (a hundred keystrokes and a save write no entry; one move writes one intent and one outcome); then the far agent's relay seat after its own research. Its reds stand at the carrier's #/the-reds. Its authority reads stand on the face's sealed identity anchor, so it builds after Wave C lands the anchor (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the controller's lean); the relay seat's own research wave follows it. Lead: a Sonnet Episkopos with a Sol and a Copilot seat. I. Built, PR #99, 2026-10-26 (kit `docs/pono/i1-intent-lane`): `@intents-<tag>` stands as the fifth face plane, registered by a signed `plane` act and never projected to disk; each entry signs under its own domain over the signed-act image, the intent id hashing issuer, verb, arguments and nonce; a device stands down on an answered slot, a single-effect verb addressed to a class or "any device" refuses at issue and an unpinned one waits on an `asks` gate whose `answer` names the atom; the winner reads by preference, then the lowest `H(atom ‖ intent id)`, with every duplicate kept visible; claims, takeover and causal voids read no clock, a finite `every` names a roster act on `@persona` and waits while its reader lacks it, and the persona root, the face's operator key, signs the release that outranks a claim; the face-join summons rides the face's plane (`lares intent issue|show|ask|answer|claim|takeover|release|cancel|supersede --face N`), the daemon-doc verb retired, and the effect door fences the pinned hearth and the operation id before any re-key, so a second hearth refuses and a replay returns its grant; the daemon wiki shows intents through a read-only pane; the rubric witness reads a seeded duplicate before trusting its zero. The far agent's relay seat passes to `I2`.
